http protocol does a three way handshake between the browser and the server
1. Browser wants to connect
2. Server approves
3. Broswer connects


Websockets and WebRTC creates persistent connections

WebSockets provide a way to establish a persistent, full-duplex communication (two-way communication) channel over a single TCP connection between the client (typically a web browser) and the server.

Server can push you events on it own


ChatApp - can use long polling as well, instead of websockets
